<Base title="About Howloop" description="Why Howloop publishes free Australian money tools, who is responsible for its content, and how calculations, sources and corrections are handled.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">THE PURPOSE BEHIND THE NUMBERS</span><h1>A little clarity for<br/>everyday money questions.</h1><p>Howloop is an independent educational project for people planning their savings and home-loan repayments in Australia.</p></header>
<article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 18 September 2026</p>
<section><h2>Why this site exists</h2><p>A large future balance can hide how much you need to contribute. An attractive bank rate can hide a condition. A lower loan balance does not tell you how much interest you have saved. Howloop makes those parts visible so you can ask better questions about your next step.</p><p>The site combines practical tools with explanations you can read before and after using them. It is built around Australian dollars, Australian sources and ordinary planning questions.</p></section>
<section id="publisher"><h2>Who publishes Howloop</h2><p>Howloop is the publishing name used for this website and its money guides. The site operator is responsible for selecting what is published, maintaining the tools and responding to corrections. Content is not presented as the work of an accredited financial-advice firm.</p><p>AI tools assist with drafting, code and mathematical checks. No independent review by a licensed financial adviser is claimed. A publication date, source-check date or passing software test is not a professional endorsement. The <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> explains these distinctions.</p></section>
<section><h2>What makes the tools useful</h2><ul><li><strong>Show the parts.</strong> Savings results separate deposits and interest. Mortgage results compare a baseline with your offset and extra repayments.</li><li><strong>Show the assumptions.</strong> We publish formulas, timing conventions and exclusions alongside examples.</li><li><strong>Show the source.</strong> Bank data has a retrieval date and links back to public provider information. A listing is not a recommendation.</li><li><strong>Let you try again.</strong> Change an input, compare a result and save a plan on your own device if you choose.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>Our role and limits</h2><p>Howloop is not a bank, lender, broker or personal financial-advice service. We do not arrange products, assess your eligibility or connect to your accounts. We cannot determine what is suitable for your circumstances. For a decision that needs personal advice, consult an appropriately qualified professional.</p></section>
<section><h2>Funding and independence</h2><p>The current money tools are free, with no account registration, paid rankings or affiliate product links. Advertising may support the site in future. Commercial placements would need to be labelled and kept separate from calculations and editorial explanations. Provider order in the bank explorer is alphabetical.</p></section>
<section><h2>Corrections and accountability</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> to report a problem, with a page address and a sample calculation or official source. Material changes are recorded in <a href="/updates">updates and corrections</a> and the affected guide. You can also inspect the <a href="/methodology">calculation methods</a> and <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Our earlier everyday guides</h2><p>Howloop previously published household and everyday how-to guides. Those pages remain in a clearly labelled <a href="/guides">archive</a> at their original addresses. The current library and navigation focus on Australian money education.</p></section></article></Base>
